    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d838">

                <pb facs="0779" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1074: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-15T14:00:00-03:00">May 15, 1940—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>219. Aranha received a telegram from his Ambassador at Buenos Aires<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d838-f1"/> reporting that Cantilo told him last night he now
                    considers the Argentine neutrality suggestions as “dead and liquidated.”</p>
                <p>Cantilo suggested an added paragraph to the Uruguayan protest which Rodríguez
                    Alves considered unacceptable. Cantilo then said that the Argentine would not
                    support the Uruguayan proposal unless some addition suggested by the Argentine
                    were accepted and suggested <pb facs="0780" n="768" xml:id="pg768"/> the
                    addition beginning “and reserve the right to take measures necessary for the
                    defense of their internal as well as their external interests” with which I
                    assume the Department is conversant.<anchor n="98" xml:id="d838-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Bolivian Ambassador perceives no objection to this suggested addition.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d838-f1" n="97" xml:id="d838-f1-content">
                <p>José de Paula Rodríguez Alves.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d838-f2" n="98" xml:id="d838-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 69, May 15, 11 a.m., from the Minister in Uruguay, <ref
                        target="#pg732">p. 732</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
